"""cctl (Claude Code ctl) — list, resume, read, watch and clean up Claude Code sessions.

Shows saved and open sessions with their /rename names, resumes them from any
folder, and can delete them.

Claude Code is a product of Anthropic. cctl is an unofficial utility for Claude
Code users, not made by or affiliated with Anthropic: it is only a wrapper
script that reads Claude Code's local session files and runs the `claude` CLI.

Reads transcripts from ~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl and
live-process records from ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json.

Examples:
  cctl                          # all sessions, newest first (= cctl ls)
  cctl ls -n                    # numbered, for use with resume and rm
  cctl ls -ltr                  # long format, newest at the bottom
  cctl ls -S -m 5               # the 5 biggest sessions
  cctl ls -N -f api             # renamed sessions in folders matching "api"
  cctl ls -s "login bug"        # search /rename names and AI titles
  cctl ls -m 10 --json          # newest 10, as JSON

  cctl resume my-name           # resume by /rename name, from any folder
  cctl resume -f api            # pick from sessions in folders matching "api"
  cctl resume 3 -- --model opus # list number; args after -- go to claude

  cctl rm my-name               # delete by name, ID (or prefix), or number
  cctl rm -f /tmp/x --all       # delete every session under a folder
  cctl rm old-test --force      # no questions asked (for scripts)

  cctl log cctl-dev --tail 10   # the last 10 turns of a session, readable
  cctl log 3 --tools | grep rm  # with tool output, piped (no pager)

  cctl watch                    # live: what every open session is doing
  cctl watch cctl-dev --verbose # one session, with full replies and errors
"""

